---
// One illustrative full-path run, played line by line (see scripts/run-reveal.ts).
---

<section id="run" class="py-16 md:py-20 max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
  <div class="max-w-2xl mb-8">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[#7A7268]">
      <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[#A855F7]"></span>
      <span>Example run</span>
      <span class="text-[#D5CCC0]">·</span>
      <span>Full path</span>
    </div>
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-[44px] font-normal text-[#26221E] leading-[1.2] mb-4">
      One run, start to finish.
    </h2>
    <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-[#6B635B] leading-relaxed">
      A feature request goes down the full path: a question, a plan, three tasks in their own worktree, and a review. An illustrative run, shortened. Real runs print more.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="run-terminal rounded-2xl bg-[#181614] border border-[#332E2A] text-[#EFEBE6] font-mono text-xs md:text-sm shadow-2xl overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Window Bar -->
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-3 bg-[#1F1C19] border-b border-[#332E2A]">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-[#E06C75]/80"></div>
        <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-[#E5C07B]/80"></div>
        <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-[#98C379]/80"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="text-[11px] text-[#8C827A]">phil · calc @ main</div>
      <div class="w-12 hidden sm:block"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="p-5 md:p-6 space-y-2.5 overflow-x-auto">
      <div data-run-line class="flex gap-2">
        <span class="text-[#C26910] font-bold">›</span>
        <span>add a --json flag to calc history</span>
      </div>
      <div data-run-line class="text-[#C084FC]">
        routed: full path <span class="text-[#8C827A]">· Jev, confidence 0.93 · 160 ms</span>
      </div>
      <div data-run-line class="text-[#D5CCC0]">
        <span class="text-[#E5C07B]">?</span> Should --json print one array, or one object per line?
        <span class="text-[#98C379]">› one array</span>
      </div>
      <div data-run-line class="text-[#D5CCC0]">
        <span class="text-[#E5C07B]">?</span> Two ways to build it: a formatter module, or a flag inside the command.
        <span class="text-[#98C379]">› a formatter module</span>
      </div>
      <div data-run-line class="text-[#E5C07B]">
        architect <span class="text-[#8C827A]">(high)</span> <span class="text-[#D5CCC0]">wrote a spec and a plan: 3 tasks</span>
      </div>
      <div data-run-line class="text-[#E5C07B]">
        critic <span class="text-[#8C827A]">(high)</span> <span class="text-[#D5CCC0]">approved the plan</span>
      </div>
      <div data-run-line class="text-[#A3998C]">
        worktree <span class="text-[#D5CCC0]">.phil/worktrees/r-7c2a</span> on branch phil/r-7c2a
      </div>
      <div data-run-line class="pl-3 border-l-2 border-[#3D3732] text-[#8C827A]">
        task 1/3 <span class="text-[#D5CCC0]">the JSON formatter</span> · implementer <span>(low)</span> · <span class="text-[#98C379]">tests pass</span>
      </div>
      <div data-run-line class="pl-3 border-l-2 border-[#3D3732] text-[#8C827A]">
        task 2/3 <span class="text-[#D5CCC0]">the --json flag</span> · implementer <span>(low)</span> · <span class="text-[#98C379]">tests pass</span>
      </div>
      <div data-run-line class="pl-3 border-l-2 border-[#3D3732] text-[#8C827A]">
        task 3/3 <span class="text-[#D5CCC0]">the docs</span> · implementer <span>(low)</span> · <span class="text-[#98C379]">checks pass</span>
      </div>
      <div data-run-line class="text-[#E5C07B]">
        reviewer <span class="text-[#8C827A]">(high)</span> <span class="text-[#D5CCC0]">0 open issues</span>
      </div>
      <div data-run-line class="pt-2 border-t border-[#2B2622] text-[#98C379]">
        ✓ branch ready · <span class="text-[#D5CCC0]">phil pr r-7c2a</span> <span class="text-[#8C827A]">· run cost $0.31</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  import { startRunReveal } from "../scripts/run-reveal";

  const run = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".run-terminal");
  if (run) startRunReveal(run);
</script>

<style>
  [data-run-line] {
    transition: opacity 0.35s ease-out;
  }

  :global(.is-pending) {
    opacity: 0;
  }
</style>
